{"vid":"goSEyGNfiPM","source":"goSEyGNfiPM.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":7.3,"txt":"Voiceover: The US Chemical Safety Board"},{"t":9.2,"txt":"is developing a new interactive training application"},{"t":12.1,"txt":"focused on OSHA's Process Safety Management"},{"t":15.3,"txt":"or PSM regulation."},{"t":24.4,"txt":"The training will cover the 14 elements of PSM"},{"t":27.7,"txt":"using the 2005 explosion"},{"t":30.8,"txt":"at BP's Texas City Refinery as a model."},{"t":38.4,"txt":"Look for it soon at CSB.gov."},{"t":43.7,"txt":"March 23, 2005, the BP Refinery in Texas City, Texas."},{"t":49.9,"txt":"Several units at the refinery had been shut down"},{"t":52.1,"txt":"for lengthy maintenance projects"},{"t":54.8,"txt":"which required nearly a thousand contractors"},{"t":57.1,"txt":"to be onsite along with BP employees."},{"t":62.1,"txt":"BP had positioned a number of portable trailers"},{"t":64.6,"txt":"close to process units for the use of"},{"t":67.2,"txt":"contractors and other maintenance workers."},{"t":70.8,"txt":"Over a period of months,"},{"t":72.2,"txt":"BP had located 10 trailers for workers"},{"t":75,"txt":"servicing the ultra-cracker unit"},{"t":77.7,"txt":"including a doublewide wood frame trailer"},{"t":79.7,"txt":"that contained 11 offices"},{"t":81.9,"txt":"and was regularly used for meetings."},{"t":84.9,"txt":"Though these trailers were"},{"t":86.2,"txt":"located near the isomerization unit,"},{"t":88.8,"txt":"the occupants were not warned the ISOM unit"},{"t":91.7,"txt":"was about to start up, a potentially hazardous operation."},{"t":97.6,"txt":"At 2:15 a.m. on March 23 overnight operators"},{"t":101.3,"txt":"began introducing flammable liquid hydrocarbons"},{"t":104.2,"txt":"known as raffinate"},{"t":106.6,"txt":"into a 170-foot tall raffinate splitter tower"},{"t":109.9,"txt":"used to distill and separate gasoline components."},{"t":115.4,"txt":"Near the base of the tower,"},{"t":117.2,"txt":"there was a single instrument"},{"t":118.8,"txt":"that measured how much liquid was inside."},{"t":121.8,"txt":"It transmitted this information"},{"t":123.5,"txt":"to both a satellite control room"},{"t":125.9,"txt":"and a central control room"},{"t":127.7,"txt":"located away from the ISOM unit."},{"t":130.7,"txt":"But this level indicator was not designed"},{"t":132.9,"txt":"to measure liquid above the 9-foot mark."},{"t":136.7,"txt":"During normal operation, the tower was only supposed"},{"t":139.6,"txt":"to contain about six and one-half feet of liquid."},{"t":143.3,"txt":"But during startups,"},{"t":144.8,"txt":"operators routinely deviated from written procedures"},{"t":147.5,"txt":"and filled the tower above the 9-foot mark,"},{"t":151.1,"txt":"concerned that if the liquid level fluctuated too low"},{"t":153.8,"txt":"it would cause costly damage to the furnace."},{"t":158.2,"txt":"At 3:09 a.m. as the liquid neared the 8-foot mark,"},{"t":162.3,"txt":"a high level alarm activated"},{"t":164.4,"txt":"and sounded in the control rooms."},{"t":167,"txt":"But as second high level alarm"},{"t":168.8,"txt":"slightly further up the tower failed to go off."},{"t":172.5,"txt":"By 3:30 a.m. the level indicator showed that"},{"t":175.3,"txt":"liquid had filled the bottom nine feet of the tower,"},{"t":178.1,"txt":"and the feed was stopped."},{"t":180.6,"txt":"The CSB later estimate that the liquid"},{"t":182.3,"txt":"was in fact at a height of 13 feet,"},{"t":186.2,"txt":"but operators could not know the actual level"},{"t":188.2,"txt":"because the indicator only measured up to nine feet."},{"t":192.5,"txt":"The lead operator had been overseeing the startup"},{"t":194.8,"txt":"from a satellite control room within the ISOM unit."},{"t":199.9,"txt":"At 5:00 a.m. he briefly updated the night board operator"},{"t":203.2,"txt":"in the central control room about the startup activities."},{"t":206.9,"txt":"The lead operator then left the refinery early,"},{"t":209.7,"txt":"an hour before the end of the shift."},{"t":213.5,"txt":"A new board operator"},{"t":214.9,"txt":"arrived in the control room around 6:00 a.m."},{"t":217.7,"txt":"to start his 30th day in a row working a 12-hour shift."},{"t":222.2,"txt":"He spoke briefly with the departing nightshift operator"},{"t":224.6,"txt":"and then read the logbook to prepare for the startup."},{"t":229,"txt":"But the logbook did not clearly indicate"},{"t":230.7,"txt":"how much liquid was already in the tower and equipment."},{"t":235.4,"txt":"And it left no instructions on routing of the liquid feed"},{"t":238.7,"txt":"and products when the startup resumed."},{"t":242.1,"txt":"Instead the control board operator only found"},{"t":244.6,"txt":"a one-line logbook entry that said,"},{"t":248,"txt":"ISOM brought in some raff to unit to pack raff with."},{"t":253.2,"txt":"At 7:15 a.m. the dayshift supervisor arrived."},{"t":257,"txt":"Because he was more than an hour late,"},{"t":259.6,"txt":"he received no formal briefing from personnel"},{"t":261.5,"txt":"on the nightshift about conditions in the ISOM unit."},{"t":266.3,"txt":"At 9:51 a.m. operators resumed the startup."},{"t":271.4,"txt":"They began recirculating the liquid feed"},{"t":273.3,"txt":"and adding more liquid to the already overfilled tower."},{"t":278.2,"txt":"As new feed was added,"},{"t":279.7,"txt":"startup procedures called for regulating the liquid level"},{"t":282.3,"txt":"in the tower using the automatic level control valve."},{"t":285.7,"txt":"But the board operator and others had received"},{"t":288.2,"txt":"conflicting instructions on routing the product."},{"t":292,"txt":"As a result,"},{"t":293,"txt":"this critical valve was left closed for several hours,"},{"t":296.7,"txt":"blocking the flow of liquid from the tower."},{"t":300.8,"txt":"A few minutes later operators lit burners on the furnace"},{"t":303.8,"txt":"to begin heating up the feed,"},{"t":305.9,"txt":"part of the normal startup process."},{"t":309.2,"txt":"While the startup was underway,"},{"t":311.1,"txt":"the day supervisor left the refinery"},{"t":312.9,"txt":"on short notice just before 11:00 a.m."},{"t":315.7,"txt":"to attend to a family medical emergency."},{"t":319.1,"txt":"Contrary to BP's own procedures,"},{"t":321.4,"txt":"no experienced supervisor was assigned to replace him."},{"t":325.9,"txt":"This left a single control board operator"},{"t":328.3,"txt":"now without a qualified supervisor"},{"t":331.1,"txt":"to run three refinery units"},{"t":333.2,"txt":"including the ISOM unit which needed close attention."},{"t":338.1,"txt":"The refinery had eliminated"},{"t":339.5,"txt":"a second board operator position"},{"t":341.5,"txt":"following corporate budget cuts"},{"t":343.4,"txt":"in 1999 after BP acquired Amoco."},{"t":348.4,"txt":"As the startup continued,"},{"t":349.8,"txt":"the tower steadily filled with liquid,"},{"t":352.2,"txt":"reaching a height of 98 feet shortly before noon,"},{"t":357.3,"txt":"more than 15 times the normal level."},{"t":361.9,"txt":"But the improperly calibrated level indicator"},{"t":364,"txt":"told operators in the control room"},{"t":366,"txt":"that the liquid was at 8.4 feet and gradually falling."},{"t":372,"txt":"Furthermore the control panel was not configured"},{"t":374.2,"txt":"to clearly warn operators of the growing danger."},{"t":377.9,"txt":"It did not display flows into and out of the tower"},{"t":380.8,"txt":"on the same screen,"},{"t":382.8,"txt":"nor did it calculate the total liquid in the tower."},{"t":387,"txt":"Meanwhile the maintenance contractors"},{"t":388.7,"txt":"who were not involved in the operation of the ISOM unit"},{"t":392,"txt":"left their work trailers to attend a company lunch,"},{"t":395.2,"txt":"celebrating a month without a lost time injury."},{"t":399.3,"txt":"At 12:41 p.m. an alarm activated"},{"t":401.8,"txt":"as the rising liquid compressed the gases"},{"t":404.8,"txt":"remaining in the top of the tower."},{"t":408.6,"txt":"Unable to understand the source of the high pressure,"},{"t":411.3,"txt":"operators opened a manual chain valve"},{"t":413.9,"txt":"that sent gases to the unit's emergency relief system,"},{"t":417.7,"txt":"a 1950's era blow down drum"},{"t":420.6,"txt":"that vented vapor directly into the atmosphere."},{"t":424.7,"txt":"Operators also turned off two burners in the furnace"},{"t":427.3,"txt":"to lower the temperature inside the tower,"},{"t":430.3,"txt":"believing this would reduce the pressure."},{"t":433.6,"txt":"Nobody knew the tower was dangerously full."},{"t":439.2,"txt":"The operators did become concerned"},{"t":441,"txt":"about the lack of flow out of the tower"},{"t":443.3,"txt":"and began opening the valve to send liquid"},{"t":445.6,"txt":"from the bottom of the tower to storage tanks."},{"t":449.1,"txt":"But this liquid was very hot."},{"t":451.8,"txt":"As it flowed through the heat exchanger,"},{"t":453.8,"txt":"it suddenly raised the temperature of the liquid"},{"t":455.8,"txt":"entering high up the tower by 141 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"t":461.9,"txt":"It was now about 1:00 p.m. Contract workers"},{"t":465,"txt":"unaware of the startup and the looming danger,"},{"t":467.8,"txt":"returned from lunch and began a meeting in the doublewide"},{"t":470.9,"txt":"trailer in the corner room closest to the blow down drum."},{"t":477.6,"txt":"Over the next few minutes, the hot feed entering the tower"},{"t":480.5,"txt":"caused the liquid inside to start to boil and swell."},{"t":485.5,"txt":"Liquid filled the tower completely"},{"t":487.3,"txt":"and began spilling into the overhead vapor line,"},{"t":490.1,"txt":"exerting great pressure"},{"t":491.3,"txt":"on the emergency relief valves 150 feet below."},{"t":495.6,"txt":"At 1:14 p.m. the three emergency valves opened,"},{"t":499.1,"txt":"sending nearly 52,000 gallons of flammable liquid"},{"t":502.6,"txt":"to the blow down drum at the other end of the ISOM unit."},{"t":506.8,"txt":"Liquid rose inside the blow down drum"},{"t":508.8,"txt":"and overflowed into a process sewer,"},{"t":511.6,"txt":"setting off alarms in the control room."},{"t":514.2,"txt":"But the high level alarm"},{"t":515.5,"txt":"on the blow down drum would fail to go off."},{"t":518.8,"txt":"None of the operators knew of the catastrophe"},{"t":520.8,"txt":"unfolding in the ISOM unit."},{"t":524.7,"txt":"As flammable hydrocarbons overfilled the blow down drum,"},{"t":528,"txt":"operators nearby saw a geyser of liquid and vapor"},{"t":531.6,"txt":"erupt from the top of the stack."},{"t":534.4,"txt":"The equivalent of nearly a tanker truck"},{"t":536.5,"txt":"full of hot gasoline"},{"t":538.2,"txt":"fell to the ground"},{"t":539.7,"txt":"and began forming a huge flammable vapor cloud."},{"t":544.4,"txt":"The vapor cloud expanded in just 90 seconds,"},{"t":547.2,"txt":"engulfing the unit"},{"t":548.5,"txt":"and the nearby trailers full of workers."},{"t":551.4,"txt":"About 25 feet from the base of the blow down drum,"},{"t":554.4,"txt":"two workers were parked in a pickup truck"},{"t":556.7,"txt":"with the engine idling."},{"t":559.1,"txt":"As flammable vapor entered the air intake,"},{"t":561.6,"txt":"the diesel engine began to race."},{"t":564.2,"txt":"The two workers fled, unable to shut off the engine."},{"t":567.5,"txt":"Moments later witnesses saw the truck backfire"},{"t":570.7,"txt":"and ignite the vapor cloud."},{"t":574.5,"txt":"Powerful explosions swept through the area."},{"t":578,"txt":"The blast pressure wave accelerated through the ISOM unit"},{"t":580.9,"txt":"causing heavy destruction and igniting fires."},{"t":585.6,"txt":"The workers inside the trailers"},{"t":587,"txt":"were right in the path of the explosions."},{"t":591,"txt":"The fires continued to burn for hours."},{"t":595.1,"txt":"12 of the 20 occupants of the doublewide trailer"},{"t":598,"txt":"were killed along with three workers in a trailer nearby."},{"t":603.2,"txt":"180 workers were injured, many with serious burns,"},{"t":606.6,"txt":"fractures or other traumatic injuries."},{"t":611,"txt":"The wood and metal frame trailers"},{"t":612.8,"txt":"were blown apart by the blasts."},{"t":615.7,"txt":"Firefighters struggled to rescue the injured"},{"t":617.7,"txt":"and recover the victims."},{"t":620.4,"txt":"50 large chemical storage tanks were damaged,"},{"t":623.7,"txt":"and the ISOM unit remained shut down"},{"t":625.9,"txt":"for more than two years."},{"t":629.7,"txt":"The disaster at BP Texas City was the most serious"},{"t":633,"txt":"refinery accident ever investigated by the CSB."}],"words":[{"t":7.316,"w":"Voiceover:"},{"t":7.316,"w":"The"},{"t":7.316,"w":"US"},{"t":7.316,"w":"Chemical"},{"t":7.316,"w":"Safety"},{"t":7.316,"w":"Board"},{"t":9.178,"w":"is"},{"t":9.178,"w":"developing"},{"t":9.178,"w":"a"},{"t":9.178,"w":"new"},{"t":9.178,"w":"interactive"},{"t":9.178,"w":"training"},{"t":9.178,"w":"application"},{"t":12.148,"w":"focused"},{"t":12.148,"w":"on"},{"t":12.148,"w":"OSHA's"},{"t":12.148,"w":"Process"},{"t":12.148,"w":"Safety"},{"t":12.148,"w":"Management"},{"t":15.339,"w":"or"},{"t":15.339,"w":"PSM"},{"t":15.339,"w":"regulation."},{"t":24.401,"w":"The"},{"t":24.401,"w":"training"},{"t":24.401,"w":"will"},{"t":24.401,"w":"cover"},{"t":24.401,"w":"the"},{"t":24.401,"w":"14"},{"t":24.401,"w":"elements"},{"t":24.401,"w":"of"},{"t":24.401,"w":"PSM"},{"t":27.737,"w":"using"},{"t":27.737,"w":"the"},{"t":27.737,"w":"2005"},{"t":27.737,"w":"explosion"},{"t":30.752,"w":"at"},{"t":30.752,"w":"BP's"},{"t":30.752,"w":"Texas"},{"t":30.752,"w":"City"},{"t":30.752,"w":"Refinery"},{"t":30.752,"w":"as"},{"t":30.752,"w":"a"},{"t":30.752,"w":"model."},{"t":38.36,"w":"Look"},{"t":38.36,"w":"for"},{"t":38.36,"w":"it"},{"t":38.36,"w":"soon"},{"t":38.36,"w":"at"},{"t":38.36,"w":"CSB.gov."},{"t":43.697,"w":"March"},{"t":43.697,"w":"23,"},{"t":43.697,"w":"2005,"},{"t":43.697,"w":"the"},{"t":43.697,"w":"BP"},{"t":43.697,"w":"Refinery"},{"t":43.697,"w":"in"},{"t":43.697,"w":"Texas"},{"t":43.697,"w":"City,"},{"t":43.697,"w":"Texas."},{"t":49.881,"w":"Several"},{"t":49.881,"w":"units"},{"t":49.881,"w":"at"},{"t":49.881,"w":"the"},{"t":49.881,"w":"refinery"},{"t":49.881,"w":"had"},{"t":49.881,"w":"been"},{"t":49.881,"w":"shut"},{"t":49.881,"w":"down"},{"t":52.074,"w":"for"},{"t":52.074,"w":"lengthy"},{"t":52.074,"w":"maintenance"},{"t":52.074,"w":"projects"},{"t":54.786,"w":"which"},{"t":54.786,"w":"required"},{"t":54.786,"w":"nearly"},{"t":54.786,"w":"a"},{"t":54.786,"w":"thousand"},{"t":54.786,"w":"contractors"},{"t":57.09,"w":"to"},{"t":57.09,"w":"be"},{"t":57.09,"w":"onsite"},{"t":57.09,"w":"along"},{"t":57.09,"w":"with"},{"t":57.09,"w":"BP"},{"t":57.09,"w":"employees."},{"t":62.097,"w":"BP"},{"t":62.097,"w":"had"},{"t":62.097,"w":"positioned"},{"t":62.097,"w":"a"},{"t":62.097,"w":"number"},{"t":62.097,"w":"of"},{"t":62.097,"w":"portable"},{"t":62.097,"w":"trailers"},{"t":64.609,"w":"close"},{"t":64.609,"w":"to"},{"t":64.609,"w":"process"},{"t":64.609,"w":"units"},{"t":64.609,"w":"for"},{"t":64.609,"w":"the"},{"t":64.609,"w":"use"},{"t":64.609,"w":"of"},{"t":67.168,"w":"contractors"},{"t":67.168,"w":"and"},{"t":67.168,"w":"other"},{"t":67.168,"w":"maintenance"},{"t":67.168,"w":"workers."},{"t":70.776,"w":"Over"},{"t":70.776,"w":"a"},{"t":70.776,"w":"period"},{"t":70.776,"w":"of"},{"t":70.776,"w":"months,"},{"t":72.21,"w":"BP"},{"t":72.21,"w":"had"},{"t":72.21,"w":"located"},{"t":72.21,"w":"10"},{"t":72.21,"w":"trailers"},{"t":72.21,"w":"for"},{"t":72.21,"w":"workers"},{"t":74.959,"w":"servicing"},{"t":74.959,"w":"the"},{"t":74.959,"w":"ultra-cracker"},{"t":74.959,"w":"unit"},{"t":77.697,"w":"including"},{"t":77.697,"w":"a"},{"t":77.697,"w":"doublewide"},{"t":77.697,"w":"wood"},{"t":77.697,"w":"frame"},{"t":77.697,"w":"trailer"},{"t":79.745,"w":"that"},{"t":79.745,"w":"contained"},{"t":79.745,"w":"11"},{"t":79.745,"w":"offices"},{"t":81.938,"w":"and"},{"t":81.938,"w":"was"},{"t":81.938,"w":"regularly"},{"t":81.938,"w":"used"},{"t":81.938,"w":"for"},{"t":81.938,"w":"meetings."},{"t":84.896,"w":"Though"},{"t":84.896,"w":"these"},{"t":84.896,"w":"trailers"},{"t":84.896,"w":"were"},{"t":86.16,"w":"located"},{"t":86.16,"w":"near"},{"t":86.16,"w":"the"},{"t":86.16,"w":"isomerization"},{"t":86.16,"w":"unit,"},{"t":88.785,"w":"the"},{"t":88.785,"w":"occupants"},{"t":88.785,"w":"were"},{"t":88.785,"w":"not"},{"t":88.785,"w":"warned"},{"t":88.785,"w":"the"},{"t":88.785,"w":"ISOM"},{"t":88.785,"w":"unit"},{"t":91.713,"w":"was"},{"t":91.713,"w":"about"},{"t":91.713,"w":"to"},{"t":91.713,"w":"start"},{"t":91.713,"w":"up,"},{"t":91.713,"w":"a"},{"t":91.713,"w":"potentially"},{"t":91.713,"w":"hazardous"},{"t":91.713,"w":"operation."},{"t":97.6,"w":"At"},{"t":97.6,"w":"2:15"},{"t":97.6,"w":"a.m."},{"t":97.6,"w":"on"},{"t":97.6,"w":"March"},{"t":97.6,"w":"23"},{"t":97.6,"w":"overnight"},{"t":97.6,"w":"operators"},{"t":101.304,"w":"began"},{"t":101.304,"w":"introducing"},{"t":101.304,"w":"flammable"},{"t":101.304,"w":"liquid"},{"t":101.304,"w":"hydrocarbons"},{"t":104.226,"w":"known"},{"t":104.226,"w":"as"},{"t":104.226,"w":"raffinate"},{"t":106.552,"w":"into"},{"t":106.552,"w":"a"},{"t":106.552,"w":"170-foot"},{"t":106.552,"w":"tall"},{"t":106.552,"w":"raffinate"},{"t":106.552,"w":"splitter"},{"t":106.552,"w":"tower"},{"t":109.929,"w":"used"},{"t":109.929,"w":"to"},{"t":109.929,"w":"distill"},{"t":109.929,"w":"and"},{"t":109.929,"w":"separate"},{"t":109.929,"w":"gasoline"},{"t":109.929,"w":"components."},{"t":115.362,"w":"Near"},{"t":115.362,"w":"the"},{"t":115.362,"w":"base"},{"t":115.362,"w":"of"},{"t":115.362,"w":"the"},{"t":115.362,"w":"tower,"},{"t":117.153,"w":"there"},{"t":117.153,"w":"was"},{"t":117.153,"w":"a"},{"t":117.153,"w":"single"},{"t":117.153,"w":"instrument"},{"t":118.833,"w":"that"},{"t":118.833,"w":"measured"},{"t":118.833,"w":"how"},{"t":118.833,"w":"much"},{"t":118.833,"w":"liquid"},{"t":118.833,"w":"was"},{"t":118.833,"w":"inside."},{"t":121.841,"w":"It"},{"t":121.841,"w":"transmitted"},{"t":121.841,"w":"this"},{"t":121.841,"w":"information"},{"t":123.546,"w":"to"},{"t":123.546,"w":"both"